Copied from github.com/fboldog/rp2350-amiga omega/ (MPL-2.0), Kick13.h removed (copyrighted ROM).
Local changes: Floppy.c, m68kops.c include "psram.h" instead of "../src/psram.h".
Local changes: chip RAM accesses in Audio.c, DMA.c, Blitter.c go through CHIPW()/chip_ptr() (platform Memory.h) so chip RAM can be split into 64 KB banks.
Local change: DMA.c dmaIdleUntil() early exits (busy blitter / executing Copper).
Local change: Blitter.c copy blits use per-blit minterm masks and a prefix-XOR area fill (bit-identical).
Local change: Floppy.c step clears /CHNG only with a disk inserted.
Local change: collisions — Chipset.c CLXCON/CLXDAT go to common/amiga/Collision.c; DMA.c feeds it bitplane blocks, armed sprites and line ends while a program reads CLXDAT.
Local change: Audio.c ADKCON attach (USExVn/USExPn): modulating channel silent, words to the next channel's VOL/PER.
Local change: Floppy.c DF1 (own ADF, track buffer, floppyConnect); DMA.c OMEGA_DYNAMIC_FIRST_LINE (image origin follows overscan bitplanes).
Local change: disk writes (DMA.c DSKLEN WRITE -> Floppy.c decodes AmigaDOS sectors into the PSRAM ADF, /WPRO from ADF location, dirty-track bitmap), ADKCON WORDSYNC off starts DMA at once.
Local change: blitter end timing — blitter_execute() still computes a blit at once, but BBUSY/INTREQ BLIT come after an estimate of its real duration (DMA.c blitTime, state 3).
Local change: Floppy.c re-arms an external drive's ID mode at every motor off (trackloaders identify DF1); motor on ends ID mode.
Local change: m68kconf.h PICO PC-relative reads are masked with ADDRESS_68K (24-bit bus).
Local change: Blitter.c line mode rewritten as the hardware steps it (A/B/C/D per pixel, error term in BLTAPT, SIGN, SUD/SUL/AUL, SING one-dot, texture rotation, registers left for chained lines).
Local change: Copper timing after vAmiga (WAIT1/2, SKIP1/2 compared at the next fetch, skipped MOVE still fetched, COPJMP after JMP1/2, cycle $E0 refused), VP7 always compared, BFD=0 waits for the blitter, next-bank WAIT only at the end of line 255.
Local change: Floppy.c floppyLineTick() — free-running /INDEX pulse (every 3125 lines) while the selected drive spins with no disk DMA.
Local change: Floppy.c external-track drives (flux images): track requests, variable track length, floppyMountExternal/TrackWanted/TrackLoaded.
Local change: Floppy.c floppyDataReady() — disk DMA waits (no words transferred) while a flux drive's track is still on its way from the master; DMA.c diskCycle() asks it.
Local change: Floppy.c floppySetState() — every selected drive takes motor/step/side, status lines wired-OR over connected drives; a port with no drive leaves /CHNG /RDY /TK0 /WPRO high.
Local change: m68kconf.h M68K_EMULATE_TRACE on (Rob Northen Copylock decrypts itself from the trace handler).
Local change: DMA.c disk DMA finds DSKSYNC at any bit position and keeps that word alignment; Chipset.c DSKLEN restarts the sync search.
Local change: Floppy.c timed tracks (flux images with a cell-length table): real-speed rotation, DSKSYNC without DMA, DSKBYTR (WORDEQUAL, BYTEREADY, data byte; byte reads wired in Chipset.c).
Local change: catch-up scheduling — DMA.c dmaRunSlice()/dmaCatchUp(): the CPU runs a slice first (up to the Copper/blitter horizon, the line end, 64 slots), custom/CIA register accesses bring the chipset up to its cycle; CPU.c raises interrupts found during a catch-up at the next instruction boundary (m68kcpu.c m68k_set_irq_deferred); m68k_end_timeslice() returns the cycles run.
Local change: DMA.c disk DMA does not search for a sync word that cannot come (no drive or no disk at the selected port).
